<div class="insight">
  <strong>Brand-specific size effects differ dramatically.</strong> Apple's price jumps from $485 at ≤40mm to $590 at 49mm+ — a 22% premium driven by the Ultra line. Garmin shows an inverted pattern at smaller sizes: ≤40mm models command $735 median (premium compact models like Venu). Samsung's pricing is relatively flat across sizes, suggesting case size is not a differentiator for Samsung buyers. The Garmin brand-level correlation of {r['case_size_brand']['Garmin']['corr']} is the highest, while Apple's {r['case_size_brand']['Apple']['corr']} reflects the bimodal Ultra vs. standard distribution rather than a linear relationship.
</div>
</section>
